        "original_id": "ec79a6ae-5794-5895-a18c-fd1966ffd5fa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Sila Region, Dar Sila, Chad, Ouaddaï Region, Sila, Djourf Al Ahmar, Libya, Sudan, Central African Republic, Cameroon, Nigeria, Niger, Markounda\n- Topics: administrative divisions, national borders\n\nFacts:\n- Sila Region, also called Dar Sila, is a region of Chad.\n- Sila Region was created in 2008 from the departments of Sila and Djourf Al Ahmar, which had previously been part of Ouaddaï Region.\n- Chad is bordered by Libya to the north, Sudan to the east, the Central African Republic to the south, Cameroon and Nigeria to the southwest, and Niger to the west.\n- Markounda is a sub-prefecture that borders Chad.",
